      "writtenOn": "2025-03-19T17:40:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I am wondering what happens if let\u0027ss say a non-Android delivered VM didn\u0027t include this in the Android.bp file. How do we enforce that every vm has this in their DICE chain?\n\nAt the end of the day its up to the authmgr-fe to build a policy correctly for their VM. We can ensure that the authmgr-fe for trusty requires this property by failing to build a policy if it is not present. Each OS will have their own policy building logic (e.g. microdroid measures all APKs as part of its dice derivation). \n\n\u003e If we want to enforce this in other Trusty VMs, we\u0027d probably need to add similar VTS.\n\nI think what we want to enforce in tests is that system vms signed with the same key cannot access each other\u0027s resources.",
